add("Hydrocarbons", "H", "Friedel-Crafts alkylation of Benzene with Methyl chloride in presence of anhydrous AlCl3 forms Toluene. Electrohile involved is:", ["Methyl carbocation (CH3⁺)", "Cl⁺", "AlCl4⁻", "Benzonium ion"], 0, "Anhydrous AlCl3 abstracts Cl⁻ from CH3Cl generating methyl electrophile CH3⁺.")
add("Hydrocarbons", "M", "Electrophilic substitution of Benzene with Conc. HNO3 and Conc. H2SO4 (Nitration) generates electrophile:", ["Nitronium ion (NO2⁺)", "Nitrosonium ion (NO⁺)", "Nitrite ion (NO2⁻)", "Nitric acid molecule"], 0, "Conc. H2SO4 protonates HNO3 to release Nitronium ion: HNO3 + 2 H2SO4 → NO2⁺ + H3O⁺ + 2 HSO4⁻.")
add("Hydrocarbons", "H", "Acidic character of hydrocarbons decreases in order:", ["HC≡CH (Ethyne) > CH2=CH2 (Ethene) > CH3-CH3 (Ethane)", "Ethane > Ethene > Ethyne", "Ethene > Ethyne > Ethane", "Ethyne > Ethane > Ethene"], 0, "Ethyne (sp hybrid, 50% s-character, high electronegativity of C) > Ethene (sp², 33%) > Ethane (sp³, 25%).")
add("Hydrocarbons", "H", "According to Huckel's Rule, a monocyclic planar conjugated system is AROMATIC if it contains:", ["(4n + 2) π electrons", "4n π electrons", "(2n + 2) π electrons", "(4n - 2) π electrons"], 0, "Huckel's rule requires planar cyclic conjugated ring with (4n + 2) π electrons (where n = 0, 1, 2...).")
add("Hydrocarbons", "M", "Hydration of Ethyne (HC≡CH) by passing into 20% H2SO4 in presence of 1% HgSO4 at 60°C yields:", ["Ethanal (Acetaldehyde)", "Ethanol", "Ethanoic acid", "Methanal"], 0, "HC≡CH + H2O --Hg²⁺/H⁺--> [CH2=CH-OH] (vinyl alcohol enol) --tautomerization--> CH3-CHO (Acetaldehyde).")
add("Hydrocarbons", "H", "Conformations of Ethane: Staggered conformation is more stable than Eclipsed conformation by 12.5 kJ/mol due to:", ["Absence of torsional strain and hyperconjugative stabilization", "Higher steric strain", "Dipole-dipole attraction", "Hydrogen bonding"], 0, "Staggered form minimizes torsional strain (repulsion between C-H bond pairs) and enjoys hyperconjugative overlap.")

