add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "M", "SN2 mechanism of nucleophilic substitution proceeds with:", ["Complete inversion of configuration (Walden inversion)", "Racemization", "Retention of configuration", "Carbocation rearrangement"], 0, "SN2 is a concerted 1-step process with backside nucleophilic attack, leading to 100% Walden Inversion.")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "H", "Reactivity of alkyl halides towards SN1 mechanism follows the order:", ["3° > 2° > 1° > CH3X", "CH3X > 1° > 2° > 3°", "2° > 3° > 1° > CH3X", "1° > 2° > 3° > CH3X"], 0, "SN1 rate depends on stability of intermediate carbocation: 3° (tertiary) > 2° (secondary) > 1° (primary) > Methyl.")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "M", "Finkelstein reaction for preparation of Alkyl iodides involves reaction of Alkyl chloride/bromide with:", ["NaI in dry Acetone", "AgF in water", "PCl5 in ether", "SOCl2 in pyridine"], 0, "R-Cl + NaI --dry acetone--> R-I + NaCl(s) (Finkelstein halide exchange reaction).")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "H", "Dehydrohalogenation of 2-Bromobutane with alcoholic KOH yields 2-Butene as major product according to:", ["Saytzeff's (Zaitsev's) Rule", "Hofmann's Rule", "Markownikoff's Rule", "Kharasch Rule"], 0, "Saytzeff's rule dictates elimination yields the more highly substituted, more stable alkene (2-Butene > 1-Butene).")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "H", "Chlorobenzene is much LESS reactive towards nucleophilic substitution than Alkyl chloride because:", ["Resonance stabilization of C-Cl bond (partial double bond character)", "sp² hybridization of phenyl carbon", "Instability of phenyl cation", "All of the above"], 3, "Resonance delocalization of Cl lone pairs gives partial double bond character, sp² carbon holds Cl tightly, and phenyl cation is unstable.")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "M", "Swarts reaction is commercially used for synthesis of:", ["Alkyl fluorides (e.g. CH3F)", "Alkyl iodides", "Alkyl chlorides", "Aryl halides"], 0, "Heating alkyl bromide/chloride with metallic fluorides (AgF, Hg2F2, SbF3) yields Alkyl fluorides (Swarts reaction).")
add("Haloalkanes & Haloarenes", "H", "Reaction of Chlorobenzene with Sodium metal in dry ether to give Diphenyl (Biphenyl) is called:", ["Fittig reaction", "Wurtz-Fittig reaction", "Wurtz reaction", "Ullmann reaction"], 0, "2 C6H5Cl + 2 Na --dry ether--> C6H5-C6H5 (Diphenyl) + 2 NaCl is Fittig reaction. (Aryl + Alkyl is Wurtz-Fittig).")
