add("Alcohols, Phenols, & Ethers", "M", "Lucas test is used to distinguish between 1°, 2°, and 3° alcohols using Lucas reagent (Conc. HCl + anhyd. ZnCl2). 3° alcohol produces turbidity:", ["Immediately at room temperature", "Within 5 minutes", "Only upon heating", "No turbidity produced"], 0, "3° alcohols form 3° carbocations instantly, producing immediate turbidity at room temp. 2° takes ~5 min; 1° requires heating.")
add("Alcohols, Phenols, & Ethers", "H", "Phenol reacts with Chloroform and aqueous NaOH followed by acidification to give Salicylaldehyde. This reaction is:", ["Reimer-Tiemann reaction", "Kolbe's reaction", "Friedel-Crafts acylation", "Cannizzaro reaction"], 0, "Reimer-Tiemann reaction generates dichlorocarbene :CCl2 electrophile, forming Salicylaldehyde (o-hydroxybenzaldehyde).")
