add("Aldehydes, Ketones, & Carboxylic Acids", "M", "Tollen's reagent used for testing Aldehydes is:", ["Ammoniacal Silver Nitrate solution [Ag(NH3)2]⁺", "Alkaline solution of CuSO4 with sodium potassium tartrate", "Acidified K2Cr2O7", "Solution of I2 in NaOH"], 0, "Tollen's reagent is freshly prepared ammoniacal silver nitrate solution [Ag(NH3)2]⁺ OH⁻, reduced by aldehydes to Silver Mirror.")
add("Aldehydes, Ketones, & Carboxylic Acids", "H", "Aldol condensation takes place between two molecules of aldehydes or ketones containing:", ["At least one α-hydrogen atom", "No α-hydrogen atom", "Halogen atom", "Aromatic ring"], 0, "Dilute NaOH abstracts α-hydrogen to form enolate ion nucleophile. Requires at least one α-H (e.g. CH3CHO).")
