add("Amines", "M", "Hofmann bromamide degradation reaction converts an Amide (RCONH2) into a Primary amine (RNH2) containing:", ["One carbon atom LESS than parent amide", "Same number of carbon atoms", "One carbon atom MORE", "Two carbon atoms less"], 0, "RCONH2 + Br2 + 4 NaOH → RNH2 + Na2CO3 + 2 NaBr + 2 H2O (degradation reduces carbon chain length by 1).")
add("Amines", "H", "Hinsberg's reagent used to distinguish 1°, 2°, and 3° amines is:", ["Benzenesulfonyl chloride (C6H5SO2Cl)", "Acetyl chloride", "Nitrous acid (HONO)", "Phenyl isocyanide"], 0, "C6H5SO2Cl reacts with 1° amine to form alkali-soluble sulfonamide; 2° amine forms alkali-insoluble sulfonamide; 3° amine does not react.")
