add("Amines", "H", "Basic strength order of Methyl substituted amines in AQUEOUS solution is:", ["(CH3)2NH > CH3NH2 > (CH3)3N > NH3  (2° > 1° > 3° > NH3)", "(CH3)3N > (CH3)2NH > CH3NH2 > NH3", "CH3NH2 > (CH3)2NH > (CH3)3N > NH3", "(CH3)2NH > (CH3)3N > CH3NH2 > NH3"], 0, "In aqueous medium, combined effect of +I effect, hydration enthalpy, and steric hindrance gives order: 2° (213) > 1° > 3° > NH3.")
add("Amines", "H", "Basic strength order of Ethyl substituted amines in AQUEOUS solution is:", ["(C2H5)2NH > (C2H5)3N > C2H5NH2 > NH3  (2° > 3° > 1° > NH3)", "(C2H5)2NH > C2H5NH2 > (C2H5)3N > NH3", "(C2H5)3N > (C2H5)2NH > C2H5NH2 > NH3", "C2H5NH2 > (C2H5)2NH > (C2H5)3N > NH3"], 0, "For ethyl substituted amines in aqueous solution, order is 2° (231) > 3° > 1° > NH3: (C2H5)2NH > (C2H5)3N > C2H5NH2 > NH3.")
add("Amines", "M", "Aniline reacts with NaNO2 and dilute HCl at 0-5°C (273-278 K) to form:", ["Benzene diazonium chloride (C6H5N2⁺ Cl⁻)", "Nitrobenzene", "Chlorobenzene", "Phenol"], 0, "Diazotization reaction of primary aromatic amine at 0-5°C yields Benzene diazonium chloride.")
add("Amines", "H", "Sandmeyer reaction converts Benzene diazonium chloride into Chlorobenzene or Bromobenzene using:", ["Cu2Cl2 / HCl or Cu2Br2 / HBr", "Cu powder / HCl", "KI / H2O", "HBF4 / Δ"], 0, "Sandmeyer reaction uses Cuprous halides (Cu2Cl2/HCl or Cu2Br2/HBr). Gattermann reaction uses Copper powder/HX.")
add("Amines", "H", "Coupling reaction of Benzene diazonium chloride with Phenol in mildly alkaline medium (pH 9-10) yields:", ["p-Hydroxyazobenzene (Orange dye)", "p-Aminoazobenzene (Yellow dye)", "Nitrobenzene", "Aniline"], 0, "C6H5N2⁺ Cl⁻ + C6H5OH --pH 9-10--> p-HO-C6H4-N=N-C6H5 (Orange azodye).")
add("Amines", "M", "Nitration of Aniline with conc. HNO3 + H2SO4 yields unexpected 47% m-Nitroaniline because:", ["In strongly acidic medium, aniline is protonated to form anilinium ion (meta-directing)", "Nitro group is meta directing", "Aniline undergoes decomposition", "Ortho position is sterically blocked"], 0, "Strong acid protonates -NH2 to -NH3⁺ (Anilinium ion), which is a powerful meta-directing group.")
add("Amines", "H", "Gabriel phthalimide synthesis is exclusively used for the preparation of:", ["Primary aliphatic amines", "Primary aromatic amines (Aniline)", "Secondary amines", "Tertiary amines"], 0, "Potassium phthalimide undergoes SN2 reaction with alkyl halide. Aryl halides cannot undergo SN2 nucleophilic attack, so aromatic 1° amines cannot be prepared.")

